build: 2026-06-28 v10.76.47 (Menu freeze + visual stability — full audit pass)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.46. Two parallel deep audits (UI-state + visuals) found the
  remaining causes of "dropdowns freeze while playing" and "visuals not stable", now fixed:
  • VISUALS (biggest): the immersive view was reading the live bio/quality signals (~10×/s)
    inside the SwiftUI layer, which rebuilt the visual + its on-screen controls ten times a
    second → stutter and flaky VJ controls. Those reads moved into the Metal draw loop
    itself (off the SwiftUI graph). Result: smooth visual, stable controls.
  • MENU: the Master-volume row read a value that automation rewrites every tick, which
    rebuilt the whole screen (closing any open dropdown). Moved into its own small view so it
    can't churn the menu screen. Plus a latent 10 Hz counter that could re-trigger the same
    freeze if ever shown is now non-observing (prevention).
  • VISUALS (jumps): the adaptive-quality governor could flip detail/frame-rate back and
    forth near a performance boundary (visible jumps); added a 4 s dwell + wider recovery
    band so it settles instead of flapping.
  All reviewed (concurrency + build): GO. No new sheets / no launch-crash surface touched.
  Test: 10.76.47 → play a take, open Compose ▸ Composition ▸ Genre/Tonart repeatedly — it
  should stay open/selectable. Open the immersive visual — it should run smooth, controls
  responsive, no detail/FPS jumping. If a dropdown STILL freezes, tell me whether it's only
  while the camera pulse is active (points to a separate fix).
